  "conclusion": "On the training-only validation slice the 14 configs span PR-AUC 0.6751 to 0.7483 (range 0.0732). The deployed C=1, class_weight=balanced scores 0.7285 +/- 0.0069 and ranks 8 of 14. Validation selects C=8, class_weight=balanced. On CONDA_valid (scored once) it reaches PR-AUC 0.8146 against 0.8246 for the deployed config: a difference of -0.0100, paired 95% CI [-0.0167, -0.0035], better in 0% of resamples. At the 0.95 alert threshold, precision/recall go from 0.965/0.363 to 0.969/0.336. The validation-best config is worse on gaming chat, so selection on the pooled (mostly general-corpus) slice does not transfer to CONDA. The deployed C=1.0 stands. For scale, the ablation shows that removing the CONDA domain data costs 0.314 PR-AUC and removing char n-grams costs 0.030. Data and representation matter more than the regularisation strength.",
